# Compiled Python is not source. CPython constant-folds the fragmented
# patterns in scripts/guard-public-vocabulary.py, so a tracked .pyc of it
# would spell every word that guard keeps out of this PUBLIC repo (it did,
# once, on 2026-09-11). The guard refuses a tracked one; this stops the stage.
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo

# Captured HTTP responses from hand-probing the API are scratch, not source.
# Six of them (m12.bin, r13/r14/r15.json, h12/h15.txt — 401 refusals and their
# response headers) rode into this PUBLIC repo's root on a `git add` during the
# cli-v2.6.14 pin (#23) and were served over raw.githubusercontent for three
# days. Nothing at this root is a .json or a .bin, so ignoring them by shape
# costs nothing and stops the next one at the stage.
/*.json
/*.bin
/h[0-9]*.txt
